<title>NETHERLANDS: Suez Nederland cuts Nedlloyd to SELL.</title>
<headline>Suez Nederland cuts Nedlloyd to SELL.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Feb 4 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Nedlloyd	  transport     54.90   Suez Nederland</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell (from hold) Savings from the merger with P&amp;O could become invisible in operating results due to overcapacity in 1997 and 1998. Expected annual growth in container traffic around 7 pct a year, but growth in container capacity of 35 pct.</p>
<p>P&amp;O Nedlloyd with four vessels of 6,000 teu-plus capacity will also be at cost disadvantage to Danish shipper Maersk which will have 15 such vessels. Cost savings due to merger will therefore not compensate for losses due to rate pressure.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS     P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	1.69    21.5    1.25</p>
<p>    1996		   1.50    31.6    1.25</p>
<p>    1997		   2.00    27.3    1.25</p>
<p>    1998		   2.50    21.8    1.25</p>
